{"slug": "motor-efficiency-classes-iec-60034", "question": "What Are Motor Efficiency Classes IE1, IE2, IE3 and IE4?", "body_html": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Motor efficiency classes IE1 to IE4 are defined by IEC 60034-30-1 and set the minimum efficiency a motor must reach for each class. Minimums for 4 pole motors at 50 Hz:</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px 0 4px;font-size:16px;\"><tr style=\"background:#1a2b4a;color:#fff;\"><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Class</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Name</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">7.5 kW</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">75 kW</th></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">IE1</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Standard</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">86.0%</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">92.7%</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">IE2</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">High</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">88.7%</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">94.1%</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">IE3</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Premium</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">90.4%</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">95.0%</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">IE4</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Super Premium</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">92.6%</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">96.1%</td></tr></table><p style=\"margin:0;\">IE3 is the mandatory minimum in the EU, India, China and Australia for motors above 0.75 kW.</p>"}